# Every text file is LF, in the repository and in the working tree, on every
# platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with the common core.autocrlf=true setting gets
# CRLF on disk, and `gofmt -l` then reports every Go file in the repository as
# unformatted -- so `make check`, which AGENT.md requires before every commit,
# cannot pass there at all. The agent ships on Windows, so a contributor on
# Windows must be able to run the same checks as CI.
#
# Declared once for everything rather than per extension: a list of extensions
# only protects the types somebody remembered, and the file that gets it wrong
# is always the one added later.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Exceptions, where the bytes are the content and a rewrite would change what
# the file means.
#
# Transcript fixtures are compared byte for byte; a line-ending rewrite would
# change the content hashes the parser tests are pinned to.
*.jsonl -text

# A release manifest and its detached signature are the exact bytes that were
# signed. A line-ending rewrite changes them, and the signature then verifies
# nowhere -- which on a Windows clone would make the update client's own test
# fail against a release that is perfectly good.
internal/update/testdata/** -text
